#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:203
msgid "Dependencies and Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:205
msgid "Required Gazebo Systems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:207
msgid ""
"Gazebo's ROS 2 Simulation Interfaces rely on Gazebo Transport topics and "
"services exposed by Gazebo's world systems rather than reading simulation "
"state directly. In particular, [`SceneBroadcaster`](https://gazebosim.org/"
"api/sim/10/classgz_1_1sim_1_1systems_1_1SceneBroadcaster.html) "
"(`gz::sim::systems::SceneBroadcaster`) is required to synchronize world "
"state and detect simulation resets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:213
msgid ""
"By default, `SceneBroadcaster`, `UserCommands`, and `Physics` are loaded "
"automatically from Gazebo's server configuration (`server.config` or "
"`GZ_SIM_SERVER_CONFIG_PATH`). However, if your world SDF disables server "
"config plugins via `<gz:policies><include_server_config_plugins>false</"
"include_server_config_plugins></gz:policies>` (while loading other world "
"plugins) or if you use a custom `GZ_SIM_SERVER_CONFIG_PATH` that omits "
"default systems, you must explicitly include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:220
msgid ""
"`gz::sim::systems::SceneBroadcaster` — required for state synchronization "
"and reset detection. Without it, initialization fails and state-dependent "
"calls return `RESULT_OPERATION_FAILED` (`\"Required Gazebo system is "
"missing\"`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:221
msgid ""
"`gz::sim::systems::UserCommands` — required by `SpawnEntity` and "
"`DeleteEntity`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:222
msgid ""
"`gz::sim::systems::Physics` — required to compute dynamic entity poses and "
"velocities for `GetEntityState` and `SetEntityState`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:225
msgid "Update Rates, Latency, and Timeouts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:227
msgid ""
"**Nominal update rates and service latency:** Most `simulation_interfaces` "
"services wait for the next state update on `SceneBroadcaster`'s `/world/"
"<world>/state` topic before responding. By default, `SceneBroadcaster` "
"throttles these updates in wall-clock time to **60 Hz** (~16.7 ms period) "
"when simulation is running and **30 Hz** (~33.3 ms period, half of the "
"running rate) when paused. Expect up to one broadcast period of latency on "
"these calls (including `GetSimulationState` and `SetSimulationState`, which "
"read pause/iteration status from `/world/<world>/stats` but still "
"synchronize with `SceneBroadcaster`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:232
msgid ""
"**Event-triggered (off-rate) updates:** In addition to its periodic "
"schedule, `SceneBroadcaster` immediately publishes an extra state message "
"whenever simulation events occur, such as spawning or deleting entities, "
"setting entity poses/twists, removing components, or resetting/rewinding "
"time. During active events, the state publish rate can temporarily exceed 60 "
"Hz / 30 Hz and service calls may unblock sooner than one nominal period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:238
msgid ""
"**Avoid setting `<state_hertz>` too low:** If you override `<state_hertz>` "
"on the `SceneBroadcaster` plugin in your SDF, keep in mind that the paused "
"rate is half of `<state_hertz>` and `simulation_interfaces` times out after "
"**1 second** (`1000 ms`) while waiting for the next state message. Setting "
"`<state_hertz>` ≤ `2.0` (when paused) or ≤ `1.0` (when running) can cause "
"calls to fail with `\"Timed out while waiting for updated Gazebo state\"` "
"whenever no simulation events occur."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:242
msgid ""
"**Stepping feedback rate:** `StepSimulation` and the `SimulateSteps` action "
"track completed steps from `/world/<world>/stats`, which Gazebo publishes at "
"**10 Hz** (100 ms period) independently of `SceneBroadcaster`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:245
msgid "Common Issues and Quirks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:247
msgid ""
"**Brief delay querying velocities after spawning an entity:** Right after "
"`SpawnEntity` succeeds, velocity tracking is enabled on the new model's "
"canonical link via `/world/<world>/control/state`. Calling `GetEntityState` "
"immediately before the server processes that update, steps physics, and "
"broadcasts the next state can temporarily fail or report zero velocity. "
"Enabling velocity tracking on all canonical links can also add overhead in "
"worlds with many models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:252
msgid ""
"**Avoid spawning entities concurrently with `ResetSimulation`:** Reset "
"completion is detected through `/world/<world>/scene/info`, which "
"`SceneBroadcaster` also publishes whenever a new entity is added to the "
"world. Spawning an entity at the same time as `ResetSimulation` can cause "
"reset detection to trigger early."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:256
msgid ""
"**Ensure the server steps on startup in custom setups:** `SceneBroadcaster` "
"only advertises its state topic and service after the first simulation "
"update step, and initial state synchronization blocks until a step runs. The "
"`gzserver` node handles this automatically; if you embed the simulation "
"interfaces alongside a custom `gz::sim::Server`, make sure the server "
"executes an initial step or is already running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:260
msgid ""
"**Single-world and top-level model scope:** Only the first world reported by "
"Gazebo (`/gazebo/worlds`) is managed. `GetEntities` and `GetEntitiesStates` "
"return top-level models only (nested models are excluded), and "
"`GetEntityState` expects a model entity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:264
msgid "Known Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:266
msgid ""
"Only an empty string or \"world\" can be used in the `frame_id` field of "
"`PoseStamped` messages. We plan to add support for using frames known to "
"`Tf` in the future."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:267
msgid "Entity namespaces are not supported by the `SpawnEntity` service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:268
msgid ""
"When spawning an entity, if `SpawnEntity.allow_renaming` is set to `true` "
"and a rename occurs in Gazebo, the new name is not returned in the `Result` "
"object return by the `SpawnEntity` service."
msgstr ""
